(2, 52, 'A ventilated patient''s SpO2 drops from 96% to 88% acutely. Using a systematic differential for displacement, obstruction, pneumothorax, and equipment failure, the nurse should assess for all of these EXCEPT:', '["Tube displacement or dislodgement", "Airway obstruction from secretions", "Pneumothorax", "Recent oral care"]'::jsonb, 3),
(2, 53, 'What percentage of chest injuries are managed WITHOUT surgery?', '["20%", "50%", "80%", "100%"]'::jsonb, 2),
(2, 54, 'Inhaled nitric oxide is used in pulmonary hypertensive crisis primarily because it:', '["Selectively dilates the pulmonary vasculature with minimal systemic hypotension", "Increases systemic vascular resistance", "Acts as a potent bronchoconstrictor", "Directly increases myocardial contractility"]'::jsonb, 0),
