(2, 58, 'A patient with pulmonary fibrosis has restrictive lung disease. On spirometry, the nurse would expect:', '["Reduced FEV1 with a normal or increased FEV1/FVC ratio, and reduced total lung capacity", "Increased total lung capacity with a low FEV1/FVC ratio", "Normal spirometry results in all cases", "Increased FVC with normal FEV1"]'::jsonb, 0),
(2, 59, 'In patients with respiratory distress, damage to type II alveolar cells can impair which of the following key functions?', '["Immunity", "Capacitation", "Gaseous exchange", "Secretion of surfactant"]'::jsonb, 3),
(2, 60, 'In which mode of ventilator the patient will initiate his/her own breath and does not depend on ventilator. Ventilator will only assess the patient efforts.', '["AC mood", "SIMV mood", "Spontaneous mood", "VCV mood"]'::jsonb, 2),
