(2, 158, 'A subtle but important principle of re-assessment is that:', '["A goal that appears met always means the problem is fully solved", "A goal may be met on paper while the underlying problem remains unsolved", "Re-assessment is unnecessary once a goal is achieved", "Only unmet goals require re-assessment"]'::jsonb, 1),
(2, 159, 'A client with well-controlled type 2 diabetes who exercises regularly, follows a prescribed diet, and reports high energy and life satisfaction would most likely be placed toward which end of the health-illness continuum?', '["Toward the high-level wellness end", "Toward the death end", "Exactly at the neutral, disease-free point only", "Outside the continuum, since a chronic disease disqualifies wellness placement"]'::jsonb, 0),
