(2, 166, 'A researcher wants to test whether a new positioning technique reduces pressure ulcer incidence. The dependent variable in this study would be:', '["The positioning technique used", "Pressure ulcer incidence, since it is the outcome being measured", "The patient''s age", "The researcher''s experience level"]'::jsonb, 1),
(2, 167, 'Vulnerable research subjects include all of the following EXCEPT:', '["Children", "Prisoners", "Healthy working adults", "The physically/mentally challenged"]'::jsonb, 2),
(2, 168, 'Which is NOT a probability sampling method?', '["Simple random sampling", "Cluster sampling", "Stratified random sampling", "Convenience sampling"]'::jsonb, 3),
(2, 169, 'A nurse wants to implement a new evidence-based practice change on the unit based on a research finding. The most appropriate first step is to:', '["Implement the change immediately unit-wide with no evaluation", "Critically appraise the evidence, involve relevant stakeholders, and consider a structured pilot with evaluation before wider rollout", "Ignore the research since current practice has always worked", "Implement changes based on personal opinion alone, without reference to evidence"]'::jsonb, 1),
