(3, 152, 'A nurse writes the goal: "Client will ambulate 30 meters with a walker by discharge on 07/28/2026." Which SMART element is reflected by the phrase "by discharge on 07/28/2026"?', '["Specific", "Measurable", "Achievable", "Time-bound"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 153, 'Phaneuf''s nursing audit tool evaluates nursing care under seven functions, which include all of the following EXCEPT:', '["Application and execution of physician''s legal orders", "Observation of symptoms and reactions", "Supervision of the patient", "Approval of hospital annual budget"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 154, 'A charge nurse asked why a particular protocol works considers several possible explanations and weighs evidence for and against each rather than accepting the first explanation offered. This reflects:', '["Open-mindedness combined with analysis", "Overconfidence", "Avoidance of the question", "Conformity to peer opinion"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 155, 'Evaluation in the nursing process is best described as:', '["A one-time final step only", "An ongoing procedure of re-assessment", "Something done only by physicians", "Unrelated to the original care plan"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 156, 'Which activity best describes the evaluation phase?', '["Interpret data and identify client problems", "Establish short- and long-term goals", "Reassess and compare outcomes with the set objectives", "Carry out nursing procedures and document"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 157, 'Copy-pasting a previous nursing note into today''s entry without verifying current accuracy risks:', '["Improved efficiency with no downside", "Documentation errors and propagation of outdated or inaccurate information (''note bloat'')", "Better legal protection", "Faster patient discharge"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 158, 'How can nurses contribute to quality assurance efforts?', '["By ignoring feedback from patients", "By working independently of their colleagues", "By participating in quality improvement initiatives and adhering to best practices", "By prioritizing speed over accuracy"]'::jsonb, 2),
