(3, 160, 'A Nurse at HMC asked a patient to verbalise if he understood the information given during nursing care to the client according to a devised nursing care plan. During which step of the nursing process does such action take place?', '["Assessment", "Planning", "Implementation", "Evaluation"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 161, 'Effective discharge planning for a rehabilitation patient should begin:', '["Only on the day of discharge", "Early during the hospital stay, involving the patient, family, and multidisciplinary team", "After the patient has already left the facility", "Without involving the patient''s family"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 162, 'The goal of quality assurance in nursing is to:', '["Reduce the cost of care", "Meet the minimum legal standards of care", "Continuously improve patient care and outcomes", "Ensure nurses follow all orders without question"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 163, 'The final step of the research process is typically considered to be', '["Disseminating or reporting the research findings to relevant audiences", "Formulating the research hypothesis", "Reviewing related literature", "Selecting the sample"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 164, 'Number of ICU admissions per month at a hospital is an example of which scale of measurement?', '["Nominal", "Ordinal", "Interval", "Ratio"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 165, 'A study finds a statistically significant but very small difference between two treatments (e.g. a 1% difference in outcome) in a very large sample. This illustrates the important distinction between:', '["Statistical significance and clinical significance/relevance", "Reliability and validity, which are unrelated concepts here", "Qualitative and quantitative research", "Ethics and methodology"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 166, 'The Latin term ''Ibid'' is used when citing:', '["The same work, the same page as just cited", "The same work, a different page from the last citation", "A completely different, unrelated work", "Only works published this year"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 167, 'In defining the scope of a study, which is NOT necessarily indicated?', '["The period of study", "The population of study", "The setting of the study", "The significance of the study"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 168, 'Process of research means the following EXCEPT', '["Identifying a problem", "Defining the problem in precise terms in unambiguous terms", "Making policies", "Designing the research"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 169, 'A core ethical requirement in human subjects research is that participation must be:', '["Mandatory for all eligible patients", "Voluntary, based on informed consent, without coercion", "Compensated financially regardless of consent", "Determined solely by the researcher"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 170, 'The Belmont Report''s 3 core ethical principles are:', '["Autonomy, Beneficence, Justice", "Consent, Privacy, Fairness", "Honesty, Accuracy, Transparency", "Safety, Dignity, Respect"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 171, 'Which measure of central tendency is appropriate for nominal (categorical) data, such as the most common blood group among patients in a ward?', '["Mean", "Median", "Mode", "Standard deviation"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 172, 'Common electronic databases for nurse researchers include all EXCEPT:', '["CINAHL", "PubMed", "MEDLINE", "American Nurses Association"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 173, 'A nurse researcher wants to study the lived experience of ICU patients after discharge. The most appropriate research approach for this question is:', '["A strictly quantitative, numerical survey with no narrative data", "A qualitative approach (e.g. interviews) to capture rich, descriptive experiential data", "No research method is appropriate for this topic", "A laboratory experiment"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 174, 'A hospital''s ''departmental risk management programme'' typically includes all of the following EXCEPT:', '["Identification of common risk categories", "Incident reporting mechanisms", "Monitoring and evaluation of interventions", "Concealing incidents to protect the department''s reputation"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 175, 'The conflict resolution style where one party gives in to preserve the relationship is called:', '["Competing", "Compromising", "Accommodating", "Avoiding"]'::jsonb, 2),
