(3, 177, 'A nurse floats to an unfamiliar ICU due to staffing shortages and is assigned a complex ventilated patient. The most appropriate first action is to:', '["Refuse the assignment entirely with no discussion", "Communicate honestly about their competency level with this patient type, request orientation/support as needed, and advocate for patient safety", "Accept the assignment silently despite feeling unprepared, saying nothing", "Provide care without seeking any support or clarification"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 178, 'Which scholar introduced the functional type of organisation?', '["F.W. Taylor", "Chester Bernard", "Allen", "Max Weber"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 179, 'The major concern of an effective leader is:', '["Concern for production only", "Concern for self", "Concern for both production and employees", "Concern for employees only"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 180, 'During a mass casualty event, the charge nurse must delegate tasks rapidly to a team with mixed experience levels. The most appropriate delegation approach is to:', '["Assign tasks randomly with no regard for skill level", "Match tasks to each team member''s competency level, ensuring appropriate supervision for less experienced staff", "Assign only the most complex tasks to the least experienced staff", "Refuse to delegate anything and do all tasks personally"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 181, 'The following are good qualities of a leader EXCEPT:', '["Visionary", "Knowledgeable", "Rich", "Integrity"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 182, 'Who advocated the fourteen principles of management?', '["Henri Fayol", "Frederick Taylor", "Max Weber", "Karl Marx"]'::jsonb, 0),
