(3, 184, 'Which of the following is a function of a ICU manager?', '["Bureaucracy", "Motivation", "Humility", "Oppression"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 185, 'Below are the Patient and family-focused interventions EXCEPT', '["Relieve anxiety and provide a sense of security", "Allow family to stay with patient, if possible, to alleviate anxiety", "Provide explanations and information", "Documentation of consent"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 186, 'When triaging multiple patients, a nurse practising justice should prioritise based on:', '["Personal characteristics such as wealth", "Clinical need", "Order of arrival only, regardless of severity", "Insurance status"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 187, 'The key distinction between Justice and Fairness is that:', '["Justice = rightness/what''s deserved; Fairness = impartiality/equal treatment", "They mean exactly the same thing with no difference", "Justice only applies to law, never to nursing", "Fairness only applies to financial matters"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 188, 'Applying the exact same rule to everyone regardless of their different starting points is:', '["Always guaranteed to be fair", "Justice, but not necessarily truly fair to everyone", "Never a valid ethical approach", "Only relevant in legal settings"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 189, 'The core legal/professional principle behind nursing documentation is best summarised as:', '["''If it wasn''t documented, it wasn''t done''", "Documentation is optional if care was given correctly", "Only negative events need to be documented", "Documentation can be completed weeks later without issue"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 190, 'The ethical principle of justice, as applied to resource allocation in critical care, refers to:', '["Treating all patients identically regardless of need", "Fair and equitable distribution of limited healthcare resources", "Prioritising the wealthiest patients", "Ignoring resource limitations entirely"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 191, 'Which ethical principle refers to a patient''s right to make their own healthcare decisions?', '["Beneficence", "Autonomy", "Non-maleficence", "Justice"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 192, 'Which is one of the twin Latin maxims applied in the principles of fair hearing?', '["Nemo dat quod non habet", "Ubi jus ibi remedium", "Nemo judex in causa sua", "Res ipsa loquitur"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 193, 'An advance directive is a document that:', '["Is only valid after the patient''s death", "Expresses a patient''s wishes for future medical care if they become unable to decide for themselves", "Can only be created by a physician", "Overrides all patient autonomy while the patient is conscious"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 194, 'A dying patient has Cheyne-Stokes respirations. The nurse educates the family that this is:', '["A sign of pain", "Indicative of fluid overload", "Normal at end-of-life", "Reversible with oxygen"]'::jsonb, 2),
(3, 195, 'Which nursing action best supports early identification of a TPN-related infection?', '["Assessing the catheter insertion site for redness, warmth, swelling, or drainage at each shift, along with monitoring temperature trends", "Assessing the insertion site only once weekly during dressing changes", "Relying solely on the patient''s subjective report of pain", "Checking the site only if the patient develops hypotension"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 196, 'These are risks of parenteral nutrition EXCEPT', '["Infection", "Hyperglycaemia", "Hypoglycaemia", "Vomiting"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 197, 'The ''ebb and flow'' model of the metabolic response to trauma describes which sequence?', '["An initial hypometabolic ''ebb'' phase of hypoperfusion followed by a hypermetabolic ''flow'' (catabolic) phase", "A single sustained hypermetabolic phase with no early depression", "An initial anabolic phase followed by a hypometabolic phase", "A random, unpredictable pattern with no identifiable phases"]'::jsonb, 0),
(3, 198, 'Refeeding syndrome is a risk primarily in patients who:', '["Have been well-nourished throughout admission", "Have experienced prolonged starvation or severe malnutrition before reintroducing nutrition", "Are only mildly overweight", "Have normal phosphate levels only"]'::jsonb, 1),
(3, 199, 'Contraindications to chest physiotherapy include all of the following EXCEPT:', '["Untreated pneumothorax", "Active haemoptysis", "Uncontrolled raised intracranial pressure", "Mild, stable chronic bronchitis"]'::jsonb, 3),
(3, 200, 'On the MRC muscle strength scale, a score of 0 indicates:', '["Normal power", "Movement against gravity only", "Complete paralysis, no movement", "Flicker of movement only"]'::jsonb, 2),
(4, 1, 'Intrapleural pressure is normally:', '["Equal to atmospheric pressure", "Negative relative to atmospheric pressure", "Positive relative to atmospheric pressure", "Highly variable with no consistent pattern"]'::jsonb, 1),
(4, 2, 'Which ECG change is classically associated with hypercalcemia?', '["Shortened QT interval", "Prolonged QT interval", "Peaked T waves", "Prominent U waves"]'::jsonb, 0),
(4, 3, 'How many pairs of spinal nerves arise from the human spinal cord?', '["12", "24", "31", "43"]'::jsonb, 2),
