(4, 24, 'Haematological investigations typically assess:', '["Blood cell counts, haemoglobin, and coagulation parameters", "Only urine composition", "Only stool consistency", "Only skin pigmentation"]'::jsonb, 0),
(4, 25, 'Early ECG changes of hyperkalaemia typically include:', '["Flattened T waves", "Tall, peaked T waves", "Prolonged QT interval as the earliest change", "U waves"]'::jsonb, 1),
(4, 26, 'Potassium is most abundant in which compartment?', '["Intracellular", "Extracellular", "Intravascular", "Interstitial"]'::jsonb, 0),
(4, 27, 'The following are causes of respiratory acidosis EXCEPT:', '["COPD", "Severe asthma", "Hyperventilation", "Head injury"]'::jsonb, 2),
(4, 28, 'When starting a patient on opioids, the recommended protocol for preventing constipation is to:', '["Add bulk fibre to the diet", "Give enemas as needed", "Increase fluids and exercise only", "Use a bowel stimulant and a stool softener"]'::jsonb, 3),
(4, 29, 'A patient presents with widened QRS complex, hypotension, and seizures after a tricyclic antidepressant (TCA) overdose. Which treatment is indicated to counteract the cardiotoxic sodium-channel blocking effect?', '["IV sodium bicarbonate", "Flumazenil", "Naloxone", "Activated charcoal alone, with no other treatment"]'::jsonb, 0),
