(4, 31, 'A patient with Torsades de Pointes is prescribed magnesium sulfate. Which ECG change confirms efficacy?', '["Resolution of U waves", "Narrowed QRS complex", "Shortened QT interval", "Absent P waves"]'::jsonb, 2),
(4, 32, 'A patient receiving IV vancomycin develops flushing, a rash on the upper body, and hypotension shortly after the infusion starts. This presentation is most consistent with:', '["A true IgE-mediated anaphylactic reaction only", "''Red man syndrome,'' related to rapid infusion rate rather than true allergy in many cases", "Normal expected drug effect requiring no action", "Sepsis unrelated to the medication"]'::jsonb, 1),
