(4, 78, 'Which finding is most suggestive of contrast-induced nephropathy after coronary angiography?', '["Hyperkalemia occurring within minutes of injection", "Gross hematuria developing after two weeks", "Immediate anuria during the procedure", "Rise in serum creatinine within 24-72 hours of contrast exposure"]'::jsonb, 3),
(4, 79, 'A patient''s urine output is measured at 20ml over the last hour, with a weight of 70kg. This represents a urine output of approximately:', '["0.3ml/kg/hr, consistent with oliguria requiring assessment", "2ml/kg/hr, a normal finding", "5ml/kg/hr, indicating polyuria", "No clinical significance regardless of the value"]'::jsonb, 0),
(4, 80, 'A patient with a very dry mouth, skin, and mucous membranes is diagnosed with dehydration. Which intervention should the nurse perform when caring for a patient diagnosed with fluid volume deficit?', '["Obtaining the clients weight weekly at different times of the day.", "Maintaining I V therapy at the keep vein open rate.", "Monitoring arterial blood gas ABG results", "Assessing urinary intake and output"]'::jsonb, 3),
